WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.130
Here’s something to talk about

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:04.960
Every YouTube creator, or, well, almost every
YouTube creator, is faced with a Catch 22

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.670
of sorts, a pair of conflicting incentives.

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:11.180
On one hand you have YouTube’s discovery
and ranking mechanisms, for which the key

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:16.309
data points are linked to engagement measured
in percent viewed, likes, shares, and subscriptions.

00:00:16.309 --> 00:00:19.949
On the other hand you have the need for a
peer relationship to the audience, or at least

00:00:19.949 --> 00:00:22.409
the perception of that relationship.

00:00:22.409 --> 00:00:25.819
The first encourages a strong call to action,
openly asking and reminding your audience

00:00:25.819 --> 00:00:30.829
to like, share, and subscribe, but this bald-faced
self-promotion is openly at odds with a sense

00:00:30.829 --> 00:00:35.020
of approachability, since it pulls back the
curtains, so to speak, and reveals the underlying

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:37.360
asymmetrical mechanics of the relationship.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:39.450
So, how to resolve this dichotomy?

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:44.450
Well, there’s no one way, but it gives us
a good opportunity to explore the memetics

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:47.800
of advertising by working our way through
one possible solution.

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:51.070
This solution is revelation through obfuscation.

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:54.640
In other words we’re going to reveal the
mechanisms, we’re going to pull back the

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:59.290
curtain, but at the same time we’re going
to put up as many other curtains as possible

00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:02.820
to distract from the curtain that we just
pulled back.

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:08.250
Yes, my friends, we’re going into the woebegotten
lands of irony and self-deprecation.

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:14.460
Alright, down to brass tacks, how are we going
to openly ask you, the audience, to like,

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:17.270
share, and subscribe while making it palatable?

00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:19.310
We’re going to turn it into a joke.

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:22.359
This joke will make it seem funny, like we’re
putting distance between ourselves and the

00:01:22.359 --> 00:01:26.749
incentives that are operating on us, however
the underlying operative and actionable idea

00:01:26.749 --> 00:01:33.429
will still be planted and the notion of interacting
with that idea will be recontextualized as

00:01:33.429 --> 00:01:35.000
an extension of the joke.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:39.780
That means you’ll be more likely to like,
share, and subscribe.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:43.149
So with all that in mind, what if we played
off the repetitive, mantra-like nature of

00:01:43.149 --> 00:01:47.950
like-share-subscribe and amped up the almost
cultish reverence?

00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:51.209
Like Share Subscribe

00:01:51.209 --> 00:01:54.020
Like Share Subscribe

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:55.909
That could work.

00:01:55.909 --> 00:01:59.209
What if we tried outright re-painting it with
existing religious iconography?

00:01:59.209 --> 00:02:04.689
Do you have a few minutes to talk about another
testament of like/share/subscribe?

00:02:04.689 --> 00:02:06.640
Maybe not the flavour we’re looking for.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:11.610
May you be blessed with the peace of like,
share, and subscribe!

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:17.080
Alright, I think we’re on the right track,
let’s take that one and combine it with

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:18.100
the snuggy monk.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:25.060
Go in peace, my children, in the name of like,
share, and subscribe, amen.

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:30.340
That’s some pretty solid obfuscation, with
a double bonus of creating a baked in atmosphere

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:32.620
of community, vis a vis spiritual initiation.

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:36.560
There’s no accident that so many of the
largest YouTube creators, and community leaders,

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:39.720
have names for their followers.

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:41.700
The Foldable Army, or Team Foldy.

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:45.120
But, this is where it all risks turning into
a quagmire.

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:50.210
It’s really easy to get bogged down in cynicism,
seeing the same actions that are so often

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:55.180
coldly exercised by massive corporations,
and ascribing the same disengaged profit motives

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:57.260
to people who just want to entertain some
people.

00:02:57.260 --> 00:03:00.630
The lines get really blurry, was it the chicken
or the egg?

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:04.400
Are we in a space where sincere individuals
are adopting and adapting the exploitative

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:08.620
mechanisms of corporations in order to succeed
in an environment where those are the rules

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:13.400
of engagement, or are corporations hijacking
the emotional structures of authentic community

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:14.980
in order to sell more soap?

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:16.130
Why not both?

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:20.570
How do we tell the two apart, where’s the
line where one grows into the other, and is

00:03:20.570 --> 00:03:24.980
it even possible to engage authentically with
another person through a displaced and asymmetrical

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:26.570
medium like YouTube?

00:03:26.570 --> 00:03:30.460
Is our cynical resistance to the idea that
we are a marketing demographic breeding an

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:34.530
air of irony that serves to do little more
than prevent us from engaging with content

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:38.890
in an authentic manner, building a wall of
feigned indifference that only separates us

00:03:38.890 --> 00:03:42.960
from our true selves, even if opening up would
leave us vulnerable to being exploited by

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:47.180
the capitalist systems that we inhabit, and
in suggesting that we allow ourselves to be

00:03:47.180 --> 00:03:51.481
vulnerable am I serving to cut through years
of defensive baggage for our own good, or

00:03:51.481 --> 00:03:55.850
simply serving the needs of a capitalist hegemony
by priming you to be more receptive to incoming

00:03:55.850 --> 00:03:56.850
messages?

00:03:56.850 --> 00:04:01.510
That… is quite possibly something for each
of us to decide on our own, but I would encourage

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:03.600
everyone to avoid becoming too cynical.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:08.970
We all need to do what we need to do to get
by, and sometimes that means dressing distasteful,

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:12.900
but necessary, things up in a silly costume
and making them do a little dance for our

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:13.900
amusement.

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:19.650
So, go in peace, my children, in the name
of like, share, and subscribe, amen.

